# Two `=` in one projection (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | project a = b = c
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..27
  PIPELINE@0..26
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    PROJECT_OP@9..26
      IDENT@9..16 "project"
      WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@17..26
        NAME@17..18
          IDENT@17..18 "a"
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        EQ@19..20 "="
        WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
        BIN_EXPR@21..26
          NAME_REF@21..22
            IDENT@21..22 "b"
          WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
          EQ@23..24 "="
          WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
          NAME_REF@25..26
            IDENT@25..26 "c"
  WHITESPACE@26..27 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:24
  |
1 | from T | project a = b = c
  |                        ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `b == c`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from T | project a = b == c
which parses without errors
